course: dictionary
lesson: 3178
title: Meet the emu
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can learn a new word by reading the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues. «Not all birds can fly: penguins, ostriches, emus and kiwis are birds that can't.» The list tells you that an emu is a bird that cannot fly.
explain: Sentences also give you details. «The emu is the second tallest bird, up to about 1.9 metres, and runs at around 50 kilometres per hour.» Second tallest means only the ostrich is taller. Up to about and around mean the numbers are rough, not exact.
explain: To check a meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word. «All birds can fly» is false, because an emu is a bird that cannot fly. The sentence «most birds can fly» is true, so the context helps you see the difference.
fact: An emu is a very large bird from Australia that cannot fly but can run very fast.
fact: An emu is the second-tallest bird in the world, after the ostrich.
fact: «A mob of emus» is a group of emus, and «emu eggs» are the eggs they lay.
fact: In emu families, the father sits on the eggs for about 8 weeks, hardly eating.
fact: The emu appears on Australia's coat of arms, together with the kangaroo.
exercise: An emu is a very large bird from Australia. What can an emu NOT do? | Live in Australia | *Fly | Run very fast | Be very large
exercise: «The emu is the second tallest bird, up to about 1.9 metres.» Which bird is taller than the emu? | A kiwi | A dingo | A penguin | *An ostrich
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The emu is the second tallest bird, up to about 1.9 metres» that means a rough number, not an exact one. | *about | bird | tallest | emu
test: «Emus run at around 50 kilometres per hour.» Does the word around mean the speed is exact? | Yes, it is exactly 50 | *No, it is a rough estimate | It means very slow | It is a speed for cars
test: Which statement is true? | All birds can fly | Emus can fly over the sea | *Most birds can fly, but emus cannot | Penguins are not birds
exam: The sentence «in the 1932 Emu War the emus mostly won» shows us what? | *Emus were hard to beat in a fight with people | 1932 had no birds in Australia | Emus were small and weak | Emus cannot run
